WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.800
Human beings are
natural storytellers.

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:11.570
The purpose of storytelling
is to connect us together.

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:14.220
I storytell as an actor,
a director, as a writer,

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:18.260
as a producer, as
a public speaker.

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:20.540
Storytelling is one of
the primary building

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:22.550
blocks of civilization.

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:26.390
Everything that is
important to us as a species

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:28.340
has been contained in stories.

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:33.230
In this MasterClass,
I'm going to help

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:39.980
you identify your personal
story; at home, at work, in play,

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:44.210
helping make you a more
effective communicator.

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:46.070
I'm going to touch
on storytelling

00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:49.850
for children, storytelling for
adults, and public speaking.

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:52.730
I'm nervous every time
I speak in public.

00:00:52.730 --> 00:00:54.030
I'm going to say that again.

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:56.510
I've been doing
this for 45 years.

00:00:56.510 --> 00:01:02.090
Every time I open my mouth
in public, I'm nervous.

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:03.980
There is a phrase
that I love using.

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:08.180
Fear is simply
suppressed excitement.

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:10.070
We all have nervousness.

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:12.800
And suppressed excitement
is a lot easier

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:16.730
to deal with intellectually
than our fear.

00:01:16.730 --> 00:01:19.610
"This storm will pass
soon," said Papa.

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:21.920
"Would you like me
to read you a story?

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:25.430
I know just the one to
help you feel better."

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:27.950
When I was a kid,
you were either going

00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:30.380
to read a book in
my mother's home,

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:32.180
or you were going
to get hit with one.

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:33.500
It was your choice.

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:36.680
But you were going to have an
experience with the written

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:37.250
word.

00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:39.740
I come from a family of
teachers, of educators.

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:42.950
So it's my turn.

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:46.010
Storytelling is a gateway
to our imagination.

00:01:46.010 --> 00:01:52.420
We can't have a just,
equitable society

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:54.350
unless we can imagine one.

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:58.930
We are here to contribute
something mighty.

00:01:58.930 --> 00:02:03.880
And our storytelling is
the ship that we sail on.

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:09.000
I'm LeVar Burton, and this
is my MasterClass.

